  "text": "The Egyptian Mazhar A Heavy and Deep Frame Drum with Cymbals Instrument Index A tunable Egyptian Mazhar with a plastic head. © MaqamWorld Pronunciation of Mazhar The Egyptian Mazhar is a very heavy frame drum with large cymbals. It is designed for heavy pounding in a loud and diverse rhythm section, such as the one used in a Zaffa (wedding procession), where Iqa‘ Zaffa is featured. Zaffa (Wedding party) An Egyptian Zaffa (wedding party) with a large group of percussionists using a combination of Egyptian Mazhar-s, Katim -s and Tabla -s, all with synthetic heads. Explore other percussion instruments: The Riqq The Tabla The Tabl Baladi The Daff The Katim The Sagat",
